// The DOM-typed variant of tsconfig.base.json, for the packages that consume viem.
//
// The base config deliberately ships `lib: ["ES2024", "WebWorker"]` rather than `DOM`. WebWorker supplies
// every web-standard global this codebase actually uses — TextEncoder, crypto/SubtleCrypto, BufferSource,
// fetch/Response, URL, AbortController — while withholding `document`, `window`, `localStorage` and the
// HTML element tree. That difference is load-bearing: the kernel, verify, conformance and the buyer-side
// gate must run unmodified in Node, a browser, Deno, Bun and a CF Worker, and typing them against browser
// globals that do not exist in half those runtimes turns a runtime failure into a silent compile pass.
//
// viem's `ox` dependency types WebAuthn (AuthenticatorAttestationResponse, AuthenticationExtensionsClient-
// Outputs), which lives only in lib.dom.d.ts. Under `skipLibCheck: false` those declarations are checked,
// so viem's consumers need DOM. Five packages extend this file, and the fifth is the one to know about:
// the four EVM packages (binding-evm-common/-escrow/-x402/-mpp) reach viem directly, and `rail-invariants`
// reaches it TRANSITIVELY — it imports every binding at once, which is the whole point of the package, so
// it inherits the DOM requirement from the EVM ones. Extending this file is that admission, made per
// package and visible in the diff — rather than granting the whole workspace browser globals to satisfy the
// ones that drag in viem. Derive this list by grepping the extenders; it has been stale before.
//
// DOM REPLACES WebWorker here rather than joining it: the two libs redeclare the same ~200 identifiers
// (BufferSource, AlgorithmIdentifier, every GL* alias) and listing both produces thousands of TS2300
// duplicate-identifier errors from inside the lib files themselves. DOM is a superset of the web-standard
// globals WebWorker carries, so nothing is lost — only the runtime-agnosticism guarantee, which is the
// trade this file exists to make explicit.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2024", "DOM"]
  }
}
